# Build output
/bv
/dist/

# Go
*.test
*.out

# Coverage run artefacts (`task coverage`, and the CI job it mirrors)
/test.json

# The release workflow writes the GitHub release body here before invoking
# GoReleaser, which refuses to run against a dirty tree — so an untracked file
# in the repo root aborts the release before it builds anything.
/release-body.md

# Local tooling
.task/

# Per-epic scratch for subagent-driven execution: review packages and
# implementer reports. Disposable by design — the durable record is the bead
# comments in .beads/ and the git history, so `git clean -fdx` costs nothing.
/.superpowers/
